{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_readme": "models = the provider's INITIAL model list, not a permanent fallback. For refresh.mode=none providers (no verified endpoint — OAuth portals such as copilot/nous/openai-codex) it is the only source and is shown as-is. For refresh.mode=api providers it seeds the first catalog build; once a live GET /models succeeds, the live list fully replaces it (the baseline only donates display labels for ids the API still lists; membership=curated keeps the baseline shortlist instead) and subsequent live failures show the last successful live list instead. Do not rename this field to fallback_models — the name 'models' is intentional. is_custom = the endpoint is the user's own server rather than a vendor API (default false; true for ollama/lmstudio): such a provider needs no API key and keeps the base_url the user configured, so switching the default model to it must not drop that base_url.",
